Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:06:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(api-server): scaffold inbound voice webhooks for ghost
 numbers

Vonage numbers are currently provisioned SMS-only (vonageClient.searchNumbers
requests features: "SMS"), and there was no voice webhook at all - a call to
a ghost number would just hit dead air with no Answer URL configured.

Adds POST/GET /api/webhooks/voice/answer (Vonage's Answer URL - must return
NCCO describing what to do with the call) and POST /api/webhooks/voice/events
(call status changes), mirroring the existing SMS inbound webhook's pattern:
look up the active ghost number by MSISDN (now shared via
findActiveNumberByMsisdn, used by both SMS and voice), and push a real-time
notification to the owner via broadcastToAlias (new "voice_call_missed" wire
type) if they're online.

Actual call routing - forward to the owner's real number, voicemail, or
bridge into the app's own WebRTC calling - is a product decision, not a
technical one, and isn't made yet. The answer webhook currently just plays a
"doesn't accept calls yet" message via NCCO so the call doesn't hit dead air,
while still notifying the owner someone tried. Swapping in real routing
later is a change to the NCCO returned here, not to the plumbing.

Still needed once call routing is decided: provisioning numbers with voice
capability (features: "SMS,VOICE" or similar) and configuring a Vonage
Application with these URLs - both are Vonage-dashboard/account-side steps,
not code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
